    "lawCode": "Amd §5, Chap 77 of 2010",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8595\n\nSPONSOR: KAMINSKY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 77 of the laws of 2010, amending the environ-\nmental conservation law and the public health law relating to an envi-\nronmental facility and cancer incidence map, in relation to the effec-\ntiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would extend the cancer mapping program in New York State for\n6 years.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill would amend section 5 of chapter 77 of the laws\nof 2010 amending the environmental conservation law and the public\nhealth law relating to an environmental facility and cancer incidence\nmap, as amended by section 5c of part D of chapter 59 of the laws of\n2016, to extend, until May 1, 2028, the authority of DEC and DOH to\noversee the cancer incidence and environmental facility maps project.\n\nSection 2 of this bill would establish an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe growth of cancer clusters in New York State has become a great\nconcern. This bill would require the collection of cases of cancer\nthroughout the State. This information is collected to help physicians\nand health care professionals determine if there are any environmental,\noccupational, or social factors that could lead to certain types of\ncancer.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2015-16: S6407C (Budget) - Signed Chapter 59\n\n2009-10: S3788C (Libous) - Signed Chapter 77\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nMinimal.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
